{"name":"Hushed Auburn","hex":"#a8857a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hushed","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Very quiet; expressed using soft tones."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of hush"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hushed"},{"term":"auburn","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dark reddish-brown colour, often used to describe hair colour."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a reddish-brown colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/auburn"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hushing","blocks":[{"text":"Hushing is an ancient and historic mining method using a flood or torrent of water to reveal mineral veins. The method was applied in several ways, both in prospecting for ores, and for their exploitation. Mineral veins are often hidden below soil and sub-soil, which must be stripped away to discover the ore veins. A flood of water is very effective in moving soil as well as working the ore deposits when combined with other methods such as fire-setting."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Dolaucothimap4.jpg/330px-Dolaucothimap4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hushing"},{"title":"Auburn hair","blocks":[{"text":"Auburn hair is a human hair color, a variety of red hair, most commonly described as reddish-brown in color. Auburn hair ranges in shades from medium to dark. It can be found with a wide array of skin tones and eye colors. The chemical pigments that cause the coloration of auburn hair are often pheomelanin with high levels of eumelanin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Uyghur-redhead.jpg/330px-Uyghur-redhead.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auburn_hair"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Tank_A%2C_Dol.jpg/500px-Tank_A%2C_Dol.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Tank_A%2C_Dol.jpg/1280px-Tank_A%2C_Dol.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Tank_A%2C_Dol.jpg/500px-Tank_A%2C_Dol.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Small tank A near north opencast at the Roman Dolaucothi Gold Mines in Carmarthenshire, Wales: the person is standing within the reservoir bank, which has eroded over the years","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATank_A%2C_Dol.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Tank_C%2C_Dol.jpg/500px-Tank_C%2C_Dol.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Tank_C%2C_Dol.jpg/1280px-Tank_C%2C_Dol.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Tank_C%2C_Dol.jpg/500px-Tank_C%2C_Dol.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tank C above main opencast at Dolaucothi","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATank_C%2C_Dol.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Anthonis_Mor_001.jpg/500px-Anthonis_Mor_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Anthonis_Mor_001.jpg/1280px-Anthonis_Mor_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Anthonis_Mor_001.jpg/500px-Anthonis_Mor_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Queen Mary I of England was described with either light or dark auburn hair.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnthonis_Mor_001.jpg"}],"sounds":{"auburn":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e9/En-us-Auburn.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/e/e9/En-us-Auburn.ogg/En-us-Auburn.ogg.mp3"}]}}}